// Nettle tea. There is no burnt-nettle obj anywhere in the cache, in any of the six vessels, which
// is why this rolls 1,1 - it cannot burn because there is nothing for it to burn into.
[cooking_generic_nettletea]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,bowl_nettlewater
data=cooked,bowl_nettletea
data=levelrequired,20
data=experience,520
data=successchance,1,1
data=successmessage,You boil the nettles into a bowl of tea.

// Raw rabbit threaded onto an iron spit (skill_cooking/scripts/spit_roast). Old School: Cooking 16,
// 72.5 xp, and only over a fire - a range has nowhere to rest a spit, hence cantcookmessage_range.
// The burn curve is the trout's: roast rabbit unlocks one level above trout for 2.5 xp more, and
// the two burn at much the same rate. https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Roast_rabbit
[cooking_generic_skewered_rabbit]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,spit_skewered_rabbit_meat
data=cooked,spit_roasted_rabbit_meat
data=burnt,spit_burned_rabbit_meat
data=levelrequired,16
data=experience,725
data=successchance,88,432
data=cantcookmessage_range,You need an open fire to roast the rabbit on the spit.
data=successmessage,You roast the rabbit over the fire.

// Raw chompy threaded onto the same iron spit (DeathPlateau-Bugs#77). Old School: Cooking 30,
// 100 xp, a fire and not a range - the same reason the rabbit cannot use one, there is nowhere on
// a range to rest a spit. Cooked is the Big Chompy Bird Hunting quest's own cooked_chompy and burnt
// is its ruined_chompy, which are the two names the wiki gives, so this adds a route to food that
// already exists rather than a second cooked chompy beside it.
//
// THE BURN CURVE IS TUNA'S, and that is not a guess at a neighbour: tuna unlocks at the same level
// 30 for the same 100 xp, so it is the one row in the table with both of this one's numbers.
// https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Skewered_chompy
[cooking_generic_skewered_chompy]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,spit_skewered_chompy
data=cooked,cooked_chompy
data=burnt,ruined_chompy
data=levelrequired,30
data=experience,1000
data=successchance,58,372
data=cantcookmessage_range,You need an open fire to roast the chompy on the spit.
data=successmessage,You roast the chompy over the fire.

// MALTING BARLEY, which is the first step of every ale in the game and had nowhere to happen.
// A handful of barley roasted on a range comes out as barley malt: no level, no experience, and
// it cannot be done over a fire - a cooking range is the only thing that will do it. It never
// burns, which is what successchance 1,1 means here.
// https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Barley_malt
[cooking_generic_barley_malt]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,barley
data=cooked,barley_malt
data=levelrequired,1
data=experience,0
data=successchance,1,1
data=cantcookmessage_fire,You need a range to roast the barley into malt.
data=successmessage,You roast the barley into malt.

// THE TWO EELS, which could not be cooked because nothing produced them to cook. Both spots are
// wired now (skill_fishing/scripts/fishing_spots/slimeyeel.rs2 and cavefish.rs2), and the cooked
// forms have been sitting in the Hitpoints guide and the consumption table all along.
//
// THE BURN CURVES ARE THE WIKI'S OWN PAIRS, not a curve fitted to its chart: every food page's
// {{Skilling success chart}} carries the low= and high= the game passes to stat_random, and those
// are these. Cooked slimy eel is low=63 high=382, which is 25% a try at level 1 and certain from
// 61; cave eel is low=38 high=332 - the lobster's pair, which this file already carries three times
// - 15.2% at level 1 and certain from 74. Both match the levels those two pages state in words.
// https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cooked_slimy_eel  https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cave_eel
//
// The messages are written out because the default builds itself from the cooked obj's name, and
// "You successfully cook a cooked slimy eel" is not a sentence.
[cooking_generic_slimey_eel]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,mort_slimey_eel
data=cooked,mort_slimey_eel_cooked
data=burnt,burnt_eel
data=levelrequired,28
data=experience,950
data=successchance,63,382
data=successmessage,You cook the slimy eel.
data=burnmessage,You accidentally burn the slimy eel.

[cooking_generic_cave_eel]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,raw_cave_eel
data=cooked,cave_eel
data=burnt,burnt_cave_eel
data=levelrequired,38
data=experience,1150
data=successchance,38,332
data=successmessage,You cook the cave eel.
data=burnmessage,You accidentally burn the cave eel.

// KARAMBWAN IS THE ONE FISH WITH TWO WAYS TO COOK IT, and a different food at the end of each:
// poorly for the poison the Shaikahan needs, thoroughly for the food that heals 18. This row is
// the poor cook, because it is the one anybody can do - level 1, and the only outcome there is
// until the quest is behind you. The thorough cook overrides the two fields that differ
// (skill_cooking/scripts/cooking.rs2); the roll and the burn are the same either way.
// 80xp poorly, 190xp thoroughly, 70/255 on a fire or a range:
// oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Raw_karambwan and /w/Poison_karambwan.
[cooking_generic_tbwt_raw_karambwan]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,tbwt_raw_karambwan
data=cooked,tbwt_poorly_cooked_karambwan
data=burnt,tbwt_burnt_karambwan
data=levelrequired,1
data=experience,800
data=successchance,70,255
data=successmessage,You cook the karambwan. The outside is done and the inside is not.
data=burnmessage,You accidentally burn the karambwan.

// "There is nothing to be gained from heating a burnt octopus." - the game's own line for it, and
// the reason this row exists at all: without it a burnt one answers "You can't cook that."
[cooking_generic_tbwt_burnt_karambwan]
table=cooking_generic
data=uncooked,tbwt_burnt_karambwan
data=cantcookmessage_fire,There is nothing to be gained from heating a burnt octopus.
data=cantcookmessage_range,There is nothing to be gained from heating a burnt octopus.
